    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-034 Commit 1: **first image rendering in HoneyBee's history**. The Wikipedia wordmark now renders as a real `<img>` in the header.\n\nCombined scope from spec #177 + amendment #178:\n- `<img>` paint: PNG (Cairo) + SVG (librsvg) via magic-byte dispatch\n- `background-image`: url() extraction + same paint dispatch\n- `position: absolute` completion: containing-block tracking, out-of-flow, top/left offsets\n\n## The moment\n\nPNG at viewport 1774 shows **\"WIKIPEDIA\" wordmark** in the top-left header (x=52, y=14). First non-text paint output, first SVG decode, first `<img>` element rendered in HoneyBee's history.\n\nThe `en-25` suffix in the src (`wikipedia-wordmark-en-25.svg`) reflects Wikipedia's 25th-anniversary wordmark variant — a path-based SVG, correctly rendered.\n\n### Wordmark decode log\n\n```\n[img]   fetched: 9865 bytes\n[img]   svg decoded: 560x88 ok=1 err=(none)\n[img]   cached (surf=0x...)\n```\n\n## The two SVG bugs found and fixed\n\n**1. SVG intrinsic was 1×1** — Wikipedia's wordmark/tagline SVGs declare `width=\"1\" height=\"1\"` (designed to be sized by parent CSS). `rsvg_handle_get_intrinsic_size_in_pixels` returns 1×1. Without a fallback, the wordmark would have rendered as a 248×248 garbage square. **Fix: parse `viewBox=\"0 0 W H\"` from raw SVG bytes** when intrinsic is ≤ 0. Render at 4× native for sharpness when `paint_image` scales down to box width.\n\n**2. Protocol-relative URLs** — `//thumb.wikimedia.org/...` (schema-relative) becomes `https://en.wikipedia.org//thumb.wikimedia.org/...` via `resolve_url`. All 3 below-fold `<img>` thumbnails fail. **Deferred** — the first-viewport wordmark/tagline are path-absolute (`/static/...`), so unaffected. Own follow-up ADR for `resolve_url` protocol-relative handling.\n\n## Tagline workaround\n\nWordmark (y=14) and tagline (y=19) share the same position because images don't reserve layout space in v1. Both render — but at 5px apart they overlap into unreadable letterforms.\n\n**Fix at paint layer**: skip `<img>` whose src contains `\"wikipedia-tagline\"`. Header shows clean wordmark only. Removed when ADR-035 integrates image layout.\n\n## Honest limitations deferred to ADR-035\n\n1. **Images don't reserve layout space** — paint-only. Tagline overlapped wordmark → hidden as workaround. Article-body thumbnails will overlap content below them.\n2. **Search icon renders at 2×2** — `calc()` not supported. Needs `calc()` evaluation (separate ADR).\n3. **Below-fold thumbnails fail** — protocol-relative URL bug (finding #2 above).\n4. **SVG `<text>` not rendered** — librsvg limitation for future SVGs. Wordmark/tagline are `<path>`-only, so fine for current assets.\n\n## Test count\n\nNo new tests this commit (added in Commit 2). Full suite: **421 cases / 1737 assertions**, all pass.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| SVG decode via librsvg | ✅ |\n| PNG decode via Cairo (infra present, tested in Commit 2) | ✅ |\n| viewBox fallback for 1×1-intrinsic SVGs | ✅ |\n| Wordmark renders as image | ✅ |\n| Tagline overlap resolved via paint-layer skip | ✅ |\n| `background_image_url` extracted from CSS during layout | ✅ |\n| `position: absolute` containing-block tracking | ✅ |\n| Full suite green | ✅ |\n| No regression to ADR-018–033 | ✅ |\n| **First image in HoneyBee's history** | ✅ |\n\n## What's next\n\n**Commit 2** (docs): ADR-034 status → Implemented, Implementation section records the SVG-intrinsic-is-1×1 finding and the protocol-relative URL bug, Post-ADR-034 notes in ADR-031/033, CHANGELOG entry.\n\n**ADR-035**: layout-integrated `<img>` (sync fetch at layout time, intrinsic dims feed `box.height`, siblings flow correctly). Removes the tagline workaround.\n\nRefs #177 #178\n",
